docker-compose.override.yml

# ── Secrets / local config (never commit real credentials) ──
# Blanket-ignore every environment-flavored appsettings file (Local, Production, Staging,
# whatever gets added later) so a stray one with real credentials can't be committed by
# accident. appsettings.json is checked in on purpose — it holds no secrets, only the settings that
# differ per environment, keyed by environment name. The Development exception stays for the day
# somebody wants a local override again; the file itself is gone because it had nothing left to say.
appsettings.*.json
!appsettings.json
!appsettings.Development.json
*.local.json
# Same suffix for prose: docs/access.local.md maps out who may reach which schema, which is
# a shopping list for anyone who gets hold of it.
*.local.md
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Local HTTPS dev certificate, exported from `dotnet dev-certs` — machine-specific, regenerable.
.certs/
*.pem
*.key

# ── OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ── Claude Code local session/tool state ─────────────────────
.claude/